      "doc": "The property `s.Nonempty` expresses the fact that the set `s` is not empty. It should be used\nin theorem assumptions instead of `∃ x, x ∈ s` or `s ≠ ∅` as it gives access to a nice API thanks\nto the dot notation. ",
